GAL16V8
TRIST16

nCS  nRD  A    B    NC   NC   NC   NC   NC   GND
NC   NC   NC   NC   DBEN NC   NC   Q    ROMOE VCC

DBEN.T = /nRD
DBEN.E = /nCS

/ROMOE.T = /nCS * /nRD * /A
ROMOE.E = VCC

Q.T = /nCS * B + Q * nCS + Q * B
Q.E = VCC

DESCRIPTION

galre selftest example (complex mode): DBEN is tri-stated while nCS is high and equals /nRD otherwise, so a fit
could compute ROMOE from DBEN's feedback; it must not, because DBEN floats exactly when ROMOE ignores it. Q is a
latch. Pins 5-9, 11-14, 16, 17 unconnected.
